module Core

### Immutable-share discipline. The guarded data is never mutated, so no lock is needed: a
### `Guarded[T, ReadOnly]` grants only read access (`Consulting[T]`), and `ReadOnly` is a zero-sized
### record, so the controller's `lock` field adds no overhead. This is the default discipline.
### :see: {LockPolicy}, {Guarded}
record ReadOnly obeys LockPolicy
  pass

### No-op: immutable data needs no reader lock.
routine ReadOnly.add_inspector()
  return

### No-op: immutable data needs no reader lock.
routine ReadOnly.remove_inspector()
  return

### No-op: `ReadOnly` grants no claimer (the access discipline rejects `amend`). Present only to
### complete the {LockPolicy} interface.
routine ReadOnly.add_claimer()
  return

### No-op: `ReadOnly` grants no claimer. Present only to complete the {LockPolicy} interface.
routine ReadOnly.remove_claimer()
  return

### Always succeeds immediately — immutable data is always readable, no lock to contend.
### :returns: always `true`.
routine ReadOnly.try_add_inspector() -> Bool
  return true

### Always succeeds — present only to complete the interface (`ReadOnly` has no real claimer).
### :returns: always `true`.
routine ReadOnly.try_add_claimer() -> Bool
  return true
